From: TB-RK3399ProD OpenWrt project
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: rockchip: safely scan PI7C9X2G304 switch buses

The RK3399 AXI PCIe controller can raise a synchronous external abort when
software reads configuration space for a BDF that has no completer.  The
existing valid-device filter avoids those reads only on the root bus and the
bus directly below it.

A PI7C9X2G304SV switch exposes its upstream port at device 0 and its two
downstream ports at devices 1 and 2 on the next bus.  Device 0 on that second
bus is intentionally absent.  Generic PCI enumeration probes it before the
two downstream ports, causing RK3399 to abort before the switch can be
enumerated.  An empty bus below either downstream port has the same problem.

Recognize the exact switch observed on this board.  Scan only devices 1 and 2
behind its upstream port.  Behind either downstream port, permit only device
0 and only while the port reports an active data link.  This preserves the
existing behavior for direct endpoints and all unrelated bridges while
avoiding unsafe ECAM accesses for the switch's legal sparse topology.
Poll the known downstream port for up to 180 ms before declaring it empty so
an endpoint that is still completing post-reset link training is not skipped.

---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-rockchip-host.c | 55 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 54 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-rockchip-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-rockchip-host.c
@@ -37,6 +37,9 @@
 #include "../pci.h"
 #include "pcie-rockchip.h"
 
+#define PCI_VENDOR_ID_PERICOM			0x12d8
+#define PCI_DEVICE_ID_PERICOM_PI7C9X2G304SV	0xb304
+
 static void rockchip_pcie_enable_bw_int(struct rockchip_pcie *rockchip)
 {
 	u32 status;
@@ -69,14 +72,64 @@ static void rockchip_pcie_update_txcredit_mui(struct rockchip_pcie *rockchip)
 static int rockchip_pcie_valid_device(struct rockchip_pcie *rockchip,
 				      struct pci_bus *bus, int dev)
 {
+	struct pci_dev *bridge = bus->self;
+	u16 link_status = 0;
+	int ret, retries;
+
 	/*
-	 * Access only one slot on each root port.
+	 * Access only one slot on the root port and its direct child bus.
 	 * Do not read more than one device on the bus directly attached
 	 * to RC's downstream side.
 	 */
 	if (pci_is_root_bus(bus) || pci_is_root_bus(bus->parent))
 		return dev == 0;
 
+	if (!bridge || bridge->vendor != PCI_VENDOR_ID_PERICOM ||
+	    bridge->device != PCI_DEVICE_ID_PERICOM_PI7C9X2G304SV)
+		return 1;
+
+	/*
+	 * PI7C9X2G304SV has a sparse internal switch bus.  Its upstream
+	 * port is device 0 on the parent bus, while its two downstream
+	 * ports are devices 1 and 2 on the child bus.  Probing the absent
+	 * device 0 on that child bus aborts the RK3399 AXI transaction.
+	 */
+	if (pci_pcie_type(bridge) == PCI_EXP_TYPE_UPSTREAM) {
+		if (dev == 0)
+			pci_info(bridge,
+				 "restricting secondary bus scan to switch ports 1 and 2\n");
+		return dev == 1 || dev == 2;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * A PCIe downstream port has one point-to-point device at slot 0.
+	 * Avoid the slot-0 ECAM read as well when this switch reports no
+	 * active data link.  Link Status bit 29 is implemented by the
+	 * PI7C9X2G304SV even when its optional Active Reporting Capable bit
+	 * is left at the reset value.
+	 */
+	if (pci_pcie_type(bridge) == PCI_EXP_TYPE_DOWNSTREAM) {
+		if (dev != 0)
+			return 0;
+
+		for (retries = 0; retries < 10; retries++) {
+			ret = pcie_capability_read_word(bridge, PCI_EXP_LNKSTA,
+							&link_status);
+			if (ret != PCIBIOS_SUCCESSFUL ||
+			    PCI_POSSIBLE_ERROR(link_status))
+				break;
+			if (link_status & PCI_EXP_LNKSTA_DLLLA)
+				return 1;
+			if (retries != 9)
+				msleep(20);
+		}
+
+		pci_info(bridge,
+			 "downstream link inactive (LnkSta %#06x); skipping config-space scan\n",
+			 link_status);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	return 1;
 }
 
